"""Finalize acceptance prose only after verified full command and JUnit success."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
base=Path("docs/milestones/AEO-5")
summary=json.loads((base/"evidence/acceptance-summary.json").read_text())
assert summary["local_implementation_accepted"] and summary["all_validator_commands_passed"]
result=summary["pytest"]
report=base/"AEO-5R_ACCEPTANCE_REPORT.md"
text=report.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
text=text.replace("**Implementation complete; final full-regression result pending collection. Formal runtime delivery remains unapproved and was not executed.**", "**LOCAL IMPLEMENTATION ACCEPTED: implementation and automated validation are complete. Formal runtime delivery remains unapproved and was not executed.**")
text=text.replace("- Final required full validator: running with the final 274-test inventory on a disposable database backup. Final result will replace this pending statement before delivery.", f"- Final required scripts/validate.py: **{result['tests']} passed in {result['seconds']:.2f} seconds; no failures, errors or skips. All 18 commands returned exit 0.** All {result['baseline_test_count']} original baseline test IDs remain present; {result['new_test_count']} additional tests pass. [Exact commands](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/commands.json), [JUnit](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/pytest.xml), [runner](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/runner.json), [verified summary](evidence/acceptance-summary.json).")
text=text.replace("This adds one test beyond the 274-test full-run inventory.", "That additional regression is included in the final 275-test full run.")
text=text.replace("and the old 600-second pytest wrapper timeout.", "the old 600-second pytest wrapper timeout, and an unnecessarily long custom fixture root that exceeded Windows temporary-file path limits. The normal short temporary root was restored; the affected existing contracts test passed independently before the complete rerun.")
text += "\n## Acceptance outcome\n\nThe local AEO-5R implementation and automated acceptance obligations pass. This is supported by executed code, actual full/targeted test results, preserved baseline test IDs, durable mocked delivery evidence and additive runtime migration fingerprints. It does not approve or claim a live publication, formal runtime milestone completion, merge or deployment. [Observed real runtime boundary](evidence/runtime-boundary.json).\n"
report.write_text(text,encoding="utf-8")
(base/"07-test-results.md").write_text(f"# AEO-5R actual test results\n\nFinal full validator: **{result['tests']} passed in {result['seconds']:.2f} seconds**, 0 failed, 0 errors, 0 skipped. All 18 required validator commands returned 0. All {result['baseline_test_count']} original baseline IDs are retained, with {result['new_test_count']} additional passing tests. The database used by the validator was a disposable SQLite backup.\n\n[Exact command results](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/commands.json), [full JUnit](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/pytest.xml), [wrapper](evidence/aeo5r-accepted-validation/runner.json), [verified acceptance summary](evidence/acceptance-summary.json).\n\nTargeted evidence: 101 delivery/provider/CLI/migration tests passed; 21 explicit-recovery/end-to-end/CLI checks passed; 27 provider transport checks passed; four separate-commit/AEO-2 compatibility checks passed. These overlap the final full inventory and are not added to its total.\n\nEarlier failures and corrections, including the timed-out full attempt and long custom fixture-path failure, are preserved in [attempt history](evidence/validation-attempt-history.json). No failed attempt is counted as a successful run.\n\nLive GitHub writes were not tested or performed. Mocked delivery evidence is explicitly marked simulated. [Actual mock report](evidence/mocked-end-to-end-delivery.json). [Acceptance report and limitations](AEO-5R_ACCEPTANCE_REPORT.md).\n",encoding="utf-8")
print("Acceptance report finalized from verified executed results")
